<title>USA: Royce generics ANDA gets FDA approval.</title>
<headline>Royce generics ANDA gets FDA approval.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royce Laboratories Inc said Tuesday it had received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for its abbreviated new drug application (ANDA) for propoxyphene hydrochloride and acetaminophen tablets in 65 mg/650 mg strength.</p>
<p>These are the generic equivalent of Wyeth Ayerst Laboratories's Wygesic Tablets, a narcotic pain reliever. Wyeth Ayerst is a unit of American Home Products Corp.</p>
<p>Royce makes and sells 19 generic prescription drugs in 40 dosage strengths.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
